      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we start by letting the integer be denoted by \\( x \\). According to the problem, when \\( x \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ x = 15k + 7 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nWe need to find the remainders when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 and by 5. First, let's consider the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3. We substitute \\( x = 15k + 7 \\) into this expression:\n\\[ x = 15k + 7 = 3(5k) + 7. \\]\nSince \\( 3(5k) \\) is a multiple of 3, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 is the same as the remainder when 7 is divided by 3. We calculate:\n\\[ 7 \\div 3 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 1, \\]\nso the remainder when 7 is divided by 3 is 1. Therefore, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, let's consider the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5. We substitute \\( x = 15k + 7 \\) into this expression:\n\\[ x = 15k + 7 = 5(3k) + 7. \\]\nSince \\( 5(3k) \\) is a multiple of 5, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5 is the same as the remainder when 7 is divided by 5. We calculate:\n\\[ 7 \\div 5 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 2, \\]\nso the remainder when 7 is divided by 5 is 2. Therefore, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nFinally, we need to find the sum of the remainders when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 and by 5. This is:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3. \\]\n\nThus, the sum of the remainders is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
