      "text": "Let's denote the integer by \\( N \\). According to the problem, when \\( N \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ N = 15k + 7 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nWe need to find the remainders when \\( N \\) is divided by 3 and by 5. First, let's find the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 3. We substitute \\( N = 15k + 7 \\) into this division:\n\\[ N \\mod 3 = (15k + 7) \\mod 3 \\]\nSince \\( 15k \\) is a multiple of 3, it leaves a remainder of 0 when divided by 3. Therefore,\n\\[ N \\mod 3 = 7 \\mod 3 = 1 \\]\nSo, the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, let's find the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 5. We substitute \\( N = 15k + 7 \\) into this division:\n\\[ N \\mod 5 = (15k + 7) \\mod 5 \\]\nAgain, \\( 15k \\) is a multiple of 5, so it leaves a remainder of 0 when divided by 5. Therefore,\n\\[ N \\mod 5 = 7 \\mod 5 = 2 \\]\nSo, the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nThe sum of the remainders when \\( N \\) is divided by 3 and by 5 is:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{3} \\]",
